        "original_id": "7b2262d3-a2f8-5f33-bc06-e13ebd1973f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Gaillardia, Browningia, Helenium\n- Taxonomy: Asteraceae, Helenieae, genera, tribe, cacti\n\nFacts:\n- Gaillardia, commonly called blanket flower, is a genus of flowering plants in the sunflower family Asteraceae that is native to North and South America.\n- Browningia is a genus of cacti with 11 accepted species and 3 unresolved species.\n- Helenieae is a tribe whose type genus is Helenium, and Gaillardia is among its best known members.",
